==Old English==

===Etymology===
From Germanic ''*swefno-'', from Indo-European ''*su̯epno-'', an extension of ''*su̯ep-'' ‘sleep’.

Cognate with Old Saxon ''sweƀan'', Old Norse ''[[svefn]]'' (Icelandic ''[[svefn]]'', Norwegian ''[[svevn]]''); the IE root also led to Ancient Greek '''{{polytonic|[[ὕπνος]]}}''', Latin ''[[somnus]]'', Old Irish ''[[suan]]'', Old Church Slavonic ''[[съпати]]'' (Russian ''[[спать]]''), Latvian ''[[sapnis]]''.

